In looking at the nethack source code I'm always surprised by two things:
one is how easy it is to read for someone without a bit of C programming
skill. The other is how the messages are coded (in English) right into the
program just like my old, old, student Pascal projects. 

Aside from JNethack, which IIRC has to essentially rewrite the game in
order to generate readable messages, why don't there seem to be other
internationalization and multilingualization projects for Nethack? I'm
really surprised there hasn't been at least a Finnish project by now. (And
for degenerate value, I'd love to try playing in Latin.) 

